            "title": "What Is CBN?",
            "use_h1": true
          }
        },
        "text_jKVR6a": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>CBN—cannabinol—is a naturally occurring cannabinoid that has become one of the most discussed plant compounds in the sleep and relaxation space. It is not synthesized directly by the hemp plant. Instead, CBN forms when THC is exposed to oxygen and light over time, gradually converting into a structurally distinct compound with its own unique properties.</p><p>At the concentrations found in hemp-derived products, CBN is non-intoxicating. It will not produce a “high.” What it will do—based on a growing body of early-stage research—is interact with your body’s <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/what-is-the-endocannabinoid-system\" target=\"_blank\">endocannabinoid system</a>in ways that are commonly discussed for nighttime relaxation and sleep maintenance. For a broader understanding of how cannabinoids work, see <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/what-are-cannabinoids\" target=\"_blank\">What Are Cannabinoids</a>?<br/><br/></p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
