        "margin_top": 68,
        "margin_bottom": 68,
        "title": "How to Use CBN: Timing and Routine",
        "max_width": 73,
        "content": "<p><strong>When: </strong>Take CBN 30–60 minutes before your target bedtime. This allows sufficient time for absorption and onset, particularly with edible formats like gummies.</p><p><strong>How: </strong>Start with the serving size recommended on your product’s label. Our sleep gummies deliver a calibrated dose of CBN alongside CBD and Reishi in each serving. For faster absorption, our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/products/cbn-full-spectrum-water-soluble-lavender-mint-sleep\" target=\"_blank\">CBN Water Soluble Tincture</a> uses nano-emulsion technology to improve bioavailability. <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/why-is-water-soluble-cbd-so-popular\" target=\"_blank\">Learn why water-soluble formats absorb faster →</a></p><p><strong>Routine stacking: </strong>CBN pairs well with basic sleep hygiene—consistent bedtime, limited screen exposure in the final hour, and a cool, dark room. Think of CBN as one element of a broader wind-down protocol, not a standalone solution.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/timing-and-routine.png",
        "image_position": "left"
      }
    },
    "wl_tabbed_image_and_text_EzzGVE": {
      "type": "wl-tabbed-image-and-text",
      "disabled": true,
      "name": "HL Tabbed Image & Text",
      "settings": {
        "cclasses": "",
        "color": "#eae1d5",
        "font_color": "#241f21",
        "link_color": "#C83D1B",
        "show_tab": true,
        "tab_color": "#5a5478",
        "margin_top": 68,
        "margin_bottom": 68,
        "title": "Safety, Quality, and What to Look For",
        "max_width": 73,
        "content": "<p>Not all hemp products are created equal. Because cannabinoid supplements are not regulated with the same rigor as pharmaceuticals, quality varies dramatically across the market. The FDA has noted that many over-the-counter CBD products contain inaccurate labeling—some with less CBD than advertised, and others with detectable THC.</p><p>When evaluating any cannabinoid product, look for third-party Certificates of Analysis (COAs) from an independent laboratory. A COA verifies the cannabinoid content, confirms the absence of harmful contaminants like heavy metals and pesticides, and validates that THC levels remain within legal limits.  <a href=\"https://lucidlabs.hemplucid.com/\" target=\"_blank\">View Hemplucid’s lab results →</a></p><p>Important: If you are pregnant, nursing, taking prescription medications, or managing a diagnosed health condition, consult a healthcare provider before using any cannabinoid product. Cannabinoids may interact with certain medications, particularly those metabolized by cytochrome P450 liver enzymes.</p><p>Cannabinoid science is advancing rapidly. We are committed to updating this page as new peer-reviewed evidence emerges. Explore our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/ingredients\" target=\"_blank\">ingredients and sourcing</a> to learn exactly what goes into every Hemplucid product, or visit our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/cbd-faq\" target=\"_blank\">CBD FAQ</a> for answers to the most common questions.<br/><br/></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/safety-quality.png",
        "image_position": "right"
      }
    },
